{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "A run saved inside a bound call keeps %!event%: Log is bound before each goal, so it runs before Work starts, saves the\nrun there and keeps it in workspace/run.plang. Resumed, the run goes on from that save inside Log and reads\n%!event!item.name% right after it — no goal starts in between — so it names the goal the saved event fired for. The\nmarker, written after the save and never in the snapshot, says the run is the resumed one; the resumed run then goes on\nthrough this goal and ends at the marker.",
  "step": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "delete file 'workspace/resumed.marker', on error 'NotFound' ignore",
